          "id": "SP_IGERNELLA_NOTABILIS",
          "name": "Igernella notabilis",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Strawberry Sponge",
          "lineage": "Igernella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Lobate conulose sponge, with large apical oscules. The sample contains seven fragments (Fig. 9 a), each about 3 cm high and 1 – 1.5 cm in diameter (Fig. 9 a 1), assumed to be from a single larger specimen. Oscules about 0.5 cm in diameter, conules 2 – 4 mm apart. Consistency soft, easily torn. Skeleton. A rectangular spongin reticulation (Fig. 9 b) of thicker ascending fibers (up to 160 µm in diameter), and thinner connecting fibres, up to 60 µm in diameter. Meshes large, 400 – 1000 µm in size. Fibers laminated and pithed, lightly cored by sand grains and broken spicules. Horny spicules (Fig. 9 c) not common, only triactines were observed, actines 310 – 700 x 16 – 25 µm.",
          "sourcedFrom": "inaturalist",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2248744",
          "children": [],
